        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:label/IssuerBlockchainNetworkParticipationAbstract/Standard/en",
          "@type": "xbrlb:Label",
          "xbrlb:labelOf": "regca:IssuerBlockchainNetworkParticipationAbstract",
          "xbrlb:labelRole": "Standard",
          "rdf:value": {
            "@value": "Issuer blockchain network participation [abstract]",
            "@language": "en"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 897
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:label/IssuerBlockchainNetworkParticipationAbstract/Documentation/en",
          "@type": "xbrlb:Label",
          "xbrlb:labelOf": "regca:IssuerBlockchainNetworkParticipationAbstract",
          "xbrlb:labelRole": "Documentation",
          "rdf:value": {
            "@value": "Proposed by Auditchain Labs; not required by the proposed rule. Blockchain Network Participation (BNP) disclosure: for each network the subject crypto asset uses, what the issuer operates and controls there (protocol, nodes and validators, stake and hash-power share, governance tokens, revenue, dependencies). Element names, datatypes and period types are unchanged from the BNP taxonomy filed with the FDIC, so facts compare across agencies. Offered under Rule 103(b)(9) (technology infrastructure, participants, and other parties and systems) and in answer to Request for Comment 28. The items reported for a period are in a table of their own, \"Rule 103(b)(9) — issuer blockchain network participation for the period\".",
            "@language": "en"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 898
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:label/OperationalControlsAndPoliciesAbstract/Standard/en",
          "@type": "xbrlb:Label",
          "xbrlb:labelOf": "regca:OperationalControlsAndPoliciesAbstract",
          "xbrlb:labelRole": "Standard",
          "rdf:value": {
            "@value": "Operational controls and policies [abstract]",
            "@language": "en"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 899
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:label/OperationalControlsAndPoliciesAbstract/Documentation/en",
          "@type": "xbrlb:Label",
          "xbrlb:labelOf": "regca:OperationalControlsAndPoliciesAbstract",
          "xbrlb:labelRole": "Documentation",
          "rdf:value": {
            "@value": "Proposed by Auditchain Labs; not required by the proposed rule. Controls over the issuer's network participation: oversight, internal audit, information barriers, and transaction-ordering safeguards.",
            "@language": "en"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 900
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:label/AffiliateBlockchainNetworkParticipationAbstract/Standard/en",
          "@type": "xbrlb:Label",
          "xbrlb:labelOf": "regca:AffiliateBlockchainNetworkParticipationAbstract",
          "xbrlb:labelRole": "Standard",
          "rdf:value": {
            "@value": "Affiliate blockchain network participation [abstract]",
            "@language": "en"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 901
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:label/AffiliateBlockchainNetworkParticipationAbstract/Documentation/en",
          "@type": "xbrlb:Label",
          "xbrlb:labelOf": "regca:AffiliateBlockchainNetworkParticipationAbstract",
          "xbrlb:labelRole": "Documentation",
          "rdf:value": {
            "@value": "Proposed by Auditchain Labs; not required by the proposed rule. Network participation by the issuer's affiliates (Rule 405 definition, adopted by Rule 100). Affiliates are related persons under Rule 100, and their participation bears on conflicts of interest under Rule 103(b)(4)(ii). The perimeter count and officer attestation make an omitted affiliate a false statement on the face of the filing. The items reported for a period are in a table of their own, \"Rule 103(b)(9) — affiliate blockchain network participation for the period\".",
            "@language": "en"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 902
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:label/AffiliatePerimeterCompletenessCertificationAbstract/Standard/en",
          "@type": "xbrlb:Label",
          "xbrlb:labelOf": "regca:AffiliatePerimeterCompletenessCertificationAbstract",
          "xbrlb:labelRole": "Standard",
          "rdf:value": {
            "@value": "Affiliate perimeter completeness certification [abstract]",
            "@language": "en"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 903
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:label/AffiliatePerimeterCompletenessCertificationAbstract/Documentation/en",
          "@type": "xbrlb:Label",
          "xbrlb:labelOf": "regca:AffiliatePerimeterCompletenessCertificationAbstract",
          "xbrlb:labelRole": "Documentation",
          "rdf:value": {
            "@value": "Grouping parent for the signature block that certifies the affiliate perimeter enumeration is complete. Sits beside regca:AffiliatePerimeterCompletenessAttestationIndicator, which states the proposition; the elements under this abstract identify the officer who certifies it and when.",
            "@language": "en"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 904
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:label/AggregatedConcentrationAndSystemicRiskAbstract/Standard/en",
          "@type": "xbrlb:Label",
          "xbrlb:labelOf": "regca:AggregatedConcentrationAndSystemicRiskAbstract",
          "xbrlb:labelRole": "Standard",
          "rdf:value": {
            "@value": "Aggregated concentration and systemic risk [abstract]",
            "@language": "en"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 905
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:label/AggregatedConcentrationAndSystemicRiskAbstract/Documentation/en",
          "@type": "xbrlb:Label",
          "xbrlb:labelOf": "regca:AggregatedConcentrationAndSystemicRiskAbstract",
          "xbrlb:labelRole": "Documentation",
          "rdf:value": {
            "@value": "Proposed by Auditchain Labs; not required by the proposed rule. Combined control by the issuer and its affiliates on each network, and whether together they could influence consensus.",
            "@language": "en"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 906
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:label/SystemicRiskAssessmentAbstract/Standard/en",
          "@type": "xbrlb:Label",
          "xbrlb:labelOf": "regca:SystemicRiskAssessmentAbstract",
          "xbrlb:labelRole": "Standard",
          "rdf:value": {
            "@value": "Systemic risk assessment [abstract]",
            "@language": "en"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 907
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:label/ThirdPartyServiceProviderArrangementsAbstract/Standard/en",
          "@type": "xbrlb:Label",
          "xbrlb:labelOf": "regca:ThirdPartyServiceProviderArrangementsAbstract",
          "xbrlb:labelRole": "Standard",
          "rdf:value": {
            "@value": "Third-party service provider arrangements [abstract]",
            "@language": "en"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 908
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca-1crypto:label/ThirdPartyServiceProviderArrangementsAbstract/Documentation/en",
          "@type": "xbrlb:Label",
          "xbrlb:labelOf": "regca:ThirdPartyServiceProviderArrangementsAbstract",
          "xbrlb:labelRole": "Documentation",
          "rdf:value": {
            "@value": "Proposed by Auditchain Labs; not required by the proposed rule. For each non-affiliate third party that provides blockchain network participation services to or for the issuer: who it is, what it does, what it is paid, and any conflicts. Carried over from Section 8 of the BNP questionnaire (questions 137-148) without questions 142-145 on yield facilitation and reserve-to-yield relationships, which are specific to payment stablecoins. The items reported for a period are in a table of their own, \"Rule 103(b)(9) — third-party service provider arrangements for the period\".",
            "@language": "en"
          },
          "xbrlb:sourceIndex": 909
        },
