          "rdfs:label": {
            "@value": "Website address for whitepapers and other offering materials",
            "@language": "en"
          },
          "dct:source": "regca-1crypto:reference/267"
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca:FunctionalUnitAbstract",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@value": "Functional unit of covered investment contract and Rule 101(e) equivalents [abstract]",
            "@language": "en"
          },
          "skos:definition": {
            "@value": "Proposed by Auditchain Labs; not required by the proposed rule. Auditchain Labs recommends (Requests for Comment 6, 7 and 31) that an issuer may define the unit of a covered investment contract as a functional unit: the subject crypto asset together with the software or other technical primitives the crypto asset invokes and that an institution needs to stand up and operate the network (for Pacioli.ai, a Pacioli Validating Node of 50,000 AUDT with its node software license). The elements below carry the crypto-asset content of each unit and the measures Rule 101(e) as proposed would report, so the Commission can read the offering either way and the per-crypto-asset arithmetic can be checked. The recommendation is intended to make the exemption easier to use for building real utility than for a token sale with nothing behind it.",
            "@language": "en"
          },
          "dct:source": [
            "regca-1crypto:reference/268",
            "regca-1crypto:reference/269",
            "regca-1crypto:reference/270",
            "regca-1crypto:reference/271",
            "regca-1crypto:reference/272",
            "regca-1crypto:reference/273"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca:SubjectCryptoAssetUnitsPerUnit",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@value": "Units of subject crypto asset in each unit of covered investment contract",
            "@language": "en"
          },
          "skos:definition": {
            "@value": "Proposed by Auditchain Labs; not required by the proposed rule. The number of units of the subject crypto asset delivered with each unit of covered investment contract as the issuer defines the unit. 1 where the unit is the crypto asset itself.",
            "@language": "en"
          },
          "dct:source": [
            "regca-1crypto:reference/274",
            "regca-1crypto:reference/275",
            "regca-1crypto:reference/276"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca:EquivalentUnitsOfSubjectCryptoAssetOffered",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@value": "Equivalent units of subject crypto asset offered (Rule 101(e)(1) measure)",
            "@language": "en"
          },
          "skos:definition": {
            "@value": "Proposed by Auditchain Labs; not required by the proposed rule. Units of covered investment contract offered times units of the subject crypto asset per unit: the number of units Rule 101(e)(1) as proposed would count.",
            "@language": "en"
          },
          "dct:source": [
            "regca-1crypto:reference/277",
            "regca-1crypto:reference/278",
            "regca-1crypto:reference/279"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca:EquivalentPurchasePricePerUnitOfSubjectCryptoAsset",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@value": "Equivalent purchase price per unit of subject crypto asset (Rule 101(e)(2) measure)",
            "@language": "en"
          },
          "skos:definition": {
            "@value": "Proposed by Auditchain Labs; not required by the proposed rule. Purchase price per unit divided by units of the subject crypto asset per unit: the price per unit Rule 101(e)(2) as proposed would report.",
            "@language": "en"
          },
          "dct:source": [
            "regca-1crypto:reference/280",
            "regca-1crypto:reference/281",
            "regca-1crypto:reference/282"
          ]
        },
        {
          "@id": "regca:PurchasersLimitedToAccreditedInvestorsIndicator",
          "rdfs:label": {
            "@value": "Purchasers limited to accredited investors",
            "@language": "en"
          },
          "skos:definition": {
            "@value": "Proposed by Auditchain Labs; not required by the proposed rule. True if the issuer restricts the offering to accredited investors as defined in Rule 501 of Regulation D, a qualification for purchasers under Rule 103(b)(2)(i); where true, the 10 percent investment limit of Rule 300(c)(2)(i)(C) does not operate because every purchaser is accredited.",
            "@language": "en"
          },
          "dct:source": [
            "regca-1crypto:reference/283",
            "regca-1crypto:reference/284",
            "regca-1crypto:reference/285",
            "regca-1crypto:reference/286"
          ]
        },
